cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this harness, its protocols or its results, please cite the repository and let us know via a GitHub Discussion or Issue."
title: "indus-script: a pre-registered test bench for Indus script decipherment claims"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Jain"
    given-names: "Arham Partap"
    affiliation: "Savir Platforms Private Limited"
    email: "arham@savir.ventures"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Savirinc/indus-script"
url: "https://github.com/Savirinc/indus-script"
license: MIT
version: "0.54.2"
date-released: "2026-10-19"
abstract: >
  Fifty-four pre-registered rounds testing proposed readings of the Indus script against
  structure-preserving shuffle nulls, impossible-language controls and a Linear B positive
  control at matched sparsity, and testing the structural statistics used to argue about
  the script against twelve real corpora at matched size. No published key passes and five
  structural instruments fail their controls; the harness, protocols, control corpora, data
  pins and failed tests are included, with a complete methods draft.
keywords:
  - Indus script
  - decipherment
  - pre-registration
  - Linear B
  - Meluhha
  - computational epigraphy
